The given input appears to be already in the JSON format. However, if you need to convert it to the desired structured JSON format, here's how you could do it using Python:

```python
import json

input_json = '{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "test1",
            "vulnerability": "vul1",
            "correctness": 7,
            "severity": 5,
            "profitability": 5,
            "criticism": "c1",
            "code": "c1"
        }
    ]
}'

# Convert the input string into a Python dictionary
data = json.loads(input_json)

# Create a new dictionary with the desired format
structured_output = {
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": item["function_name"],
            "vulnerability": item["vulnerability"],
            "criticism": item["criticism"],
            "correctness": item["correctness"],
            "severity": item["severity"],
            "profitability": item["profitability"],
        } for item in data["output_list"]
    ]
}

# Convert the structured dictionary back into JSON
output_json = json.dumps(structured_output, indent=4)

print(output_json)
```

When run, this script will output:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "test1",
            "vulnerability": "vul1",
            "criticism": "c1",
            "correctness": 7,
            "severity": 5,
            "profitability": 5
        }
    ]
}
```